title: 'codex restart-in-place execs resume on an unpersisted thread id: ''No saved session found'', then DEGRADED delivery loop (no frontend thread)'
updated_at: "2026-07-17T14:36:39Z"
---
Observed 2026-07-17 in ~/src/codename-thin, two managed Codex sessions side by side (aliases codex-ribbon-tarot-ef62 and codex-mound-tine-356d), Codex v0.144.5, model gpt-5.6-sol, launched via cx (c2c new/start codex).

## Symptom chain (identical in both sessions)

1. Launch ~20:36: app-server ready, but Codex TUI reports 'MCP client for c2c failed to start: MCP startup failed: handshaking with MCP server failed: connection closed: initialize response' + 'MCP startup incomplete (failed: c2c)'. NOTE: B224 (marked done) added a preflight for stale [mcp_servers.c2c] config — either the preflight missed this failure mode (server crashed during initialize rather than binary-missing), or the installed binary predates the fix. Needs checking; may warrant its own bug.
2. Session sat idle with '0 in / 0 out' (no turns ever ran — MCP failure meant the operator prompt never produced a turn, or the prompt was submitted right as restart fired).
3. ~00:33 launcher execs restart-in-place: 'restarting in place on thread <id>' → 'c2c resume codex <alias> --thread-id <exact_thread>' (c2c_codex_session.ml ~1163-1181).
4. Codex errors: 'ERROR: No saved session found with ID 019f6fa5-... Run codex resume without an ID to choose from existing sessions.' — the thread id captured by the delivery loop was never persisted by Codex (plausibly because zero turns ran, so no rollout file was written).
5. Resumed session then logs 'delivery loop ran DEGRADED: no frontend thread was ever loaded, so c2c mail was not auto-delivered this session (session was still supervised).' Operator lands back at the shell with a dead managed session and no delivered mail.

## Suspected root cause

restart-in-place (c2c_codex_session.ml, restart_executable/thread_id branch) trusts the delivery loop's thread_id unconditionally and execs 'resume codex <alias> --thread-id <id>' without verifying Codex actually persisted that thread (rollout file exists / codex knows the id). A thread with zero completed turns is never saved, so resume-by-id hard-fails, and the relaunched supervisor then runs degraded because no thread can load.

## Fix ideas

- Before exec-ing resume with --thread-id, verify the thread is resumable (rollout/session file exists under CODEX_HOME); if not, resume without --thread-id or start a fresh thread instead of propagating a dead id.
- Treat Codex 'No saved session found' on managed resume as a recoverable condition: fall back to fresh-thread launch (keeping alias/registration) rather than ending in DEGRADED supervision.
- Also investigate why restart-in-place fired at ~00:33 on idle sessions (scheduled restart? restart-stale? peer-triggered c2c restart?) and whether the trigger should skip sessions with zero turns.
- Re-verify B224 preflight coverage: handshake still failed at launch in both panes.

Screenshot of both panes captured in session 5d699ec4 (image cache 1.png). Repro likely: launch managed codex, let MCP handshake fail / run zero turns, then trigger restart-in-place.